<p>The pattern is clear: HyperDFlash wins on every benchmark. The largest relative gains are on math tasks (GSM8K: 3.80× vs 2.76×, +37.7%) where longer, more structured output sequences allow the block drafter to accept longer prefixes consistently. Chat (MT-Bench: 2.07× vs 1.91×, +8.4%) shows the smallest absolute gain because short, varied conversational turns limit how many consecutive draft tokens can be accepted regardless of method.</p>

<p>The Think-high mode results follow the same pattern: HyperDFlash reaches τ=3.36 and 2.53× speedup in reasoning mode (non-thinking T=0: τ=3.69, 2.80×), demonstrating robustness across both standard and extended-thinking generation styles.</p>

